  "content": "<b>Meaning/Usage</b>: Asking someone why they are so sad.\n<b>Explanation</b>: The \"blue\" in this phrase is the same \"blue\" of being sad.\n\"<b>Why so blue</b>, is everything ok?\"\n\"You look so depressed. <b>Why so blue</b>?\"\n\"<b>Why so blue?</b> Did he hurt your feelings?\"\n<b>A.</b> \"You seem a bit sad, <b>why so blue</b>?\"\n<b>B.</b> \"My girlfriend and I got into an argument and I'm sad.\"\nOther Common Sentences\n\"Why are you so sad?\"\n\"Why do you look depressed?\"",
